abstract: >
  Integrated Systems Oncology is a modular computational oncology framework composed
  of four independently validated computational simulation engines: Tumor Evolution,
  Metabolism, Epigenetics, and Synergy, with a master orchestration layer and
  project-wide validation. The framework provides seed-reproducible simulations of
  cancer-state dynamics, covering clonal evolution, metabolic dynamics, epigenetic
  regulation, and systems-level model interaction. It is designed for reproducible
  computational oncology research, education, and scientific collaboration.
